      <div>
        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">Tuesday 14 October 1806, two battles fought on the same day</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near Jena and Auerstedt, then in the Duchy of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar">Weimar</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia</a>, now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a>, the French under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> I (initially 48,000, rising to 96,000 in the area, of whom 40,000 fought) against a Prussian army under Prince Hohenlohe. At Auerstedt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-nicolas-davout">Marshal Davout</a>'s III Corps against the main Prussian army of 64,000 under the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> and King Frederick William III. Before the campaign the Prussians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> together numbered about 130,000 Prussians and 20,000 Saxons against a French force of 180,000.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The French won both battles. Prussian losses were 10,000 killed or wounded and 15,000 prisoners at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a>, and 13,000 casualties at Auerstedt against 7,052 for Davout's corps.</span></div>
        </div>
